{"title":"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859c3069d10156cc701463c822280114e2a75c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}, a_{2}, \\dots, a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd69ad8f022ee1b5894dee7cafb68305b47c9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />) be real numbers such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4e04b54c2d1f0dad88a502d7cd3313552e78b32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{1} + a_{2} + \\cdots + a_{n} \\geq n \\qquad \\mbox{and} \\qquad a_{1}^{2} + a_{2}^{2} + \\cdots + a_{n}^{2} \\geq n^{2}.\\]\" width=\"455\" height=\"19\" />\nProve that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7781411d73cce7205d212673b89180bf748f60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max(a_{1}, a_{2}, \\dots, a_{n}) \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First, suppose all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> are positive.  Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/3577ed2f8c34f0c8fad982e812743fd964a1ca09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\max(a_1, \\dotsc, a_n) \\ge \\sqrt{\\frac{a_1^2 + \\dotsb + a_n^2}{n}} \\ge \\sqrt{n} \\ge 2 .\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"43\" />\nSuppose, on the other hand, that without loss of generality,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee078bb1a2ad809ed0ae9b32af1a26c713de7de6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1 \\ge a_2 \\ge \\dotsb \\ge a_k \\ge 0 &gt; a_{k+1} \\ge \\dotsb \\ge a_n,\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\nwith <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437a4ff34c8f6a17bfa526b22fb62ed9538242df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le k &lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04d7dacf36cb476239c7c5063cef1d18a3247e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> we are done, so suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92aeb015c39fb99b48d7b22ee1f7baff817c366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 \\le2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />.  Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce74729a3835210f6a3c89a32ba17cd69d85b99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^k a_i \\le 2k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"86\" height=\"51\" />, so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e5202c11b585e83d51b3a687e17520aa1f6255.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=k+1}^n -a_i \\le 2k-n .\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"49\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a261d99f406f4b9e4f015d99b712f67725955ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> is a positive real for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/03946aa79ad2fcef25dc5ce2ddef62542addcf53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1 \\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />, it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55dd393483c1c30ec35bdfc73ff70a96cacfe52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=k+1}^n a_i^2 \\le \\left( \\sum_{i=k+1}^n-a_i \\right)^2 \\le (2k-n)^2 .\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"57\" />\nThen\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303111d3b77e8a75ce20e35e399ca479a10aff45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\max(a_1, \\dotsc, a_n)^2 &amp;\\ge \\sum_{i=1}^k a_i^2 /k \\\\ &amp;\\ge \\left( n^2 - \\sum_{i=k+1}^n a_i^2 \\right)/k \\\\ &amp;\\ge \\frac{n^2 - (2k-n)^2}{k} = 4(n-k). \\end{align*}\" width=\"368\" height=\"159\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/7400e866ec206aeeca3f416d787b8bbeed9e1b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d66f20ef66040e05e09bef6cfa8734d4cfb0f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(n-k) &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847036d259b7a1077624717c2bc2cc0bf9435f07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max(a_1, \\dotsc, a_n) \\ge \\sqrt{4} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"24\" />, as desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Assume the contrary and suppose each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is less than 2.\n</p><p>Without loss of generality let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7bea6394cbf7ca60872f169b295bb42facc9f87c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 \\le a_2 \\le a_3 \\le ... \\le a_n &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the largest integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962a682ac5a7b812453eb793e03f3505b0863a7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412f5b308789d669fe1ea892d786116fe8c62abb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> if it exists, or 0 if all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> are non-negative. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/84574de7797bc7b4e1fc52075f4d265ba60a8bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b94ea0cc3ac2d353695f157196aed47896fefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f402ae6f41e936b4a083b80d671f02af04b7a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2 &lt; \\sum_{i=1}^n 4 = 4n \\le n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"193\" height=\"48\" />, a contradiction. Hence, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d04596cf6c41e42bd12598a6a1cbad566706e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge k \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a55522dcafabe66691c4fe1c19ef617fe4067619.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^k a_i \\ge n - \\sum_{i=k+1}^n a_i &gt; n - 2(n-k) = 2k - n.\\]\" width=\"362\" height=\"52\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d8874f9128c97f7c4ebbacc64e9f9a0fdfb651dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92eca6c4646a7191efe57e94c29bc29d3dd6c976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, both sides of the inequality are non-positive, so squaring flips the sign. But we also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1af17d3b739e15bcc10044599b67af3175395822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i a_j \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13ba1bf35b5e092e520885663ef8cba152cded34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i, j \\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af2c7961d1b73475b896d26fa52c403c77e5b5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^k a_i^2 \\le \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^k a_i \\right)^2 &lt; (2k - n)^2 = 4k^2 - 4kn + n^2,\\]\" width=\"394\" height=\"57\" />\nwhich results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4f1595229b3f533a9dc6be6f37ead7289892ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^k a_i^2 + \\sum_{i=k+1}^n a_i^2 &lt; 4k^2 - 4kn + n^2 + 4(n-k) = n^2 - 4(k-1)(n-k) \\le n^2,\\]\" width=\"597\" height=\"52\" />\na contradiction to our given condition. The proof is complete.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume the contrary for maximum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34e7dcd4a992ff9902dc4303564ffd0862ffa1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />. Then, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d395ec7f0b3191aee5f994999d1d7359ede64a45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\leq M &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" /> hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/5982a5e1a02dad49526513452133a1ae4d54e7b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8ea3731c71a95c71c853c6d14663ca2fc06db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_i)(a_i - 2) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a5d6a3ab5e081ff15d4404c850612a330fad0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i^2 &lt; 2a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"21\" />. When summing over all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, that implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77bac25e39c2327f33c230145295d49cb0aef2dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 &lt; 2\\sum a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"100\" height=\"31\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/8037143985618898cba12635953d312a502f8f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum a_i &lt; 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"90\" height=\"31\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af56c18445c7475c47c043eb56ff2a67504392ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 &lt; 4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b15835991a65124d5def20e48b608d0269060e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />. However <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437c5aa3f99a1416f23b1fbf04ba01dea855c90b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+ \\neq 1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> hence a contradiction arises, and so the maximum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/01418ba09dcb128eba69523e7d1630962c0e5657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> as requested. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO\" title=\"1999 USAMO\">1999 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016205826\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 314/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1663/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9924/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.473      1 -total\n 36.89%    6.445      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 31.91%    5.575      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 29.67%    5.184      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6086:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016205826 and revision id 286602. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}